      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable why \"reclaiming\" feels like a hopeless concept when the core seems erased. If the old self is gone, maybe the focus shifts from recovering a lost thing to building something new, however small. Even within the routine, there might be tiny moments—a small interest, a single feeling—that can act as a thread to weave a different, more authentic self. You don't have to rebuild everything at once; just finding one point of resonance can be enough to break the charade.",
      "source": "target",
